PRIMARY POSITIVE
The two worlds are observationally identical under:

price
+
transfer behavior.

Functional consequence separates them.

Thus:

MUTUALLY CONSISTENT CONTROL-PLANE SIGNALS

DO NOT ESTABLISH

CAUSAL SCARCITY REALITY.

A price/transfer scarcity claim can nominate:

BE CONSERVATIVE.

But when the decision has high functional consequence,
the organism can ask:

DOES OBEYING THIS SCARCITY SIGNAL ACTUALLY IMPROVE LOCAL FUNCTION / RESOURCE OUTCOME?

OBSERVATIONAL POLICY NEGATIVE
A policy that always trusts the mutually consistent scarcity signature makes the same decision in both worlds.

It must therefore be wrong in at least one.

This is an identifiability failure,
not a threshold-tuning problem.

FUNCTIONAL CHALLENGE INTERPRETATION
The challenge does NOT attempt to prove:

THE NEIGHBOR IS MALICIOUS.

It answers a narrower local question:

IS THIS STRUCTURAL RESTRICTION FUNCTIONALLY JUSTIFIED HERE?

That is sufficient for local authority.

The source may remain:
unknown
or
untrusted

without requiring semantic fault attribution.

CAUSAL-CONSEQUENCE CONFOUND STRESS
Functional consequence can itself be confounded.

A synthetic passive environmental shift is added during the challenge.

Two mirror stresses are tested.

FALSE SCARCITY

true branch benefit:
+0.32.

passive confound:
-0.32.

Without matched control,
the observed mean benefit becomes near zero.

30,000 episodes.

UNCONTROLLED CHALLENGE

ACCEPT:
13.11%.

REJECT:
13.06%.

HOLD:
73.83%.

mean trials:
19.73.

The validator becomes mostly indecisive.

GENUINE SCARCITY

true branch benefit:
-0.32.

passive confound:
+0.32.

The same collapse occurs:

approximately:
13% accept
13% reject
74% hold.

PRIMARY CAUSAL-CONTROL NEGATIVE
FUNCTIONAL CONSEQUENCE
IS NOT AUTOMATICALLY CAUSAL CONSEQUENCE.

A changing local environment can cancel or imitate the branch effect.

MATCHED LOCAL CONTROL
Add a matched no-branch local control exposed to the same passive environmental change.

Adjusted benefit:

branch-treated consequence
-
matched untreated consequence.

Control observation noise is independent at the same primary scale.

FALSE SCARCITY + MATCHED CONTROL

correct ACCEPT:
90.53%.

incorrect REJECT:
0.46%.

HOLD:
9.01%.

mean trials:
10.28.

median:
8.

GENUINE SCARCITY + MATCHED CONTROL

correct REJECT:
90.36%.

incorrect ACCEPT:
0.50%.

HOLD:
9.14%.

mean trials:
10.34.

median:
8.

PRIMARY MATCHED-CONTROL POSITIVE
Matched causal control restores most of the discriminating power under the tested passive-confound stress.

The cost is:

more samples
and
more unresolved decisions

than the clean functional challenge.

This is expected.

RELATION TO H12 / H20 / H41
The same architectural law now appears in three places:

STRUCTURAL GROWTH:
candidate structure must earn functional value.

CONTEXT CHANGE:
candidate context must earn functional routing value.

SHARED TEMPLATE PROMOTION:
candidate template must improve regenerated function.

H51 adds:

RESOURCE SCARCITY AUTHORITY:
a high-cost structural restriction may need functional consequence when advisory and transfer channels share the same failure mode.

RELATION TO H50
H50:
typed trust prevents one bad channel from unnecessarily destroying another.

H51:
even when both channels agree,
agreement alone does not establish truth.

Thus:

TYPED TRUST
solves cross-channel interference.

FUNCTIONAL CAUSAL CONSEQUENCE
solves shared-failure identifiability.

CURRENT SCARCITY-AUTHORITY STACK
PRICE TRUST

+

TRANSFER TRUST

+

JOINT SOURCE HEALTH

+

DIRECT LOCAL RESOURCE EVIDENCE

+

TEMPORAL CONSISTENCY

->

SCARCITY PROPOSAL.

Then, when stakes justify it:

BOUNDED PROVISIONAL FUNCTIONAL CHALLENGE

+

