GENERAL PRINCIPLE
CONTROL-PLANE AGREEMENT
SHOULD NOT BE ABLE TO PERMANENTLY OVERRIDE
FUNCTIONAL REALITY.

If several advisory channels share one failure mode,
the organism needs another source of identifiability.

DECISION
AR-H51 is POSITIVE WITH A CAUSAL-CONTROL REQUIREMENT.

Supported synthetically:

- mutually consistent price and transfer manipulation can be observationally indistinguishable from real scarcity;
- a bounded provisional functional challenge separates the two strong cases at ~99.2% accuracy;
- functional consequence can itself be confounded;
- matched local controls recover most of the lost discrimination;
- unresolved/hold is preferable to forcing a decision under weak causal evidence.

Not demonstrated:

- real Yggdrasil scarcity challenge;
- safe provisional branching under mature critical structures;
- optimal challenge budget;
- real matched local control construction;
- global resource consequence;
- subtle long-horizon scarcity effects.

NEXT CLEAN QUESTION
AR-H52 — VALUE-GATED SCARCITY OVERRIDE CHALLENGE

H51 can run up to 24 paired trials to validate a suspicious scarcity signal.

That cannot be universal.

Question:

WHEN IS IT WORTH CHALLENGING SCARCITY AUTHORITY?

Use:

candidate branch value
+
price/transfer disagreement risk
+
template leverage
+
challenge cost
+
urgency
+
local resource runway

to decide:

TRUST SCARCITY

or
RUN FUNCTIONAL CHALLENGE

or
HOLD / DEFER BRANCHING.

Desired:

low-value candidate
->
do not spend expensive challenge budget.

high-value candidate suppressed by uncertain scarcity
->
challenge.

severe real runway stress
->
respect scarcity unless evidence value is very high.

This should reuse the same S4-S9 / H21-H22 evidence economy
rather than create another scheduler.

Do not execute STAB-18-R1 during this lane.

